    "evidence_text": "Statistical analysis was done using SAS 9.1.   \n\n\nRESULTS Six hundred and ninety five children with acute uncomplicated malaria participated in the study.\n\n33.8.\n\nLeucocyte count showed no correlation with age or parasite density.   \n\n\nIndividuals homozygous for alpha(+)-thalassaemia have microcytosis and an increased erythrocyte count.\n\nObjectives.\n\nTo evaluate the predictive value of thrombocytopenia in malaria.\n\nPatients and Methods.\n\nResults.\n\nIn children with malaria, high lymphocyte and low monocyte counts were independently associated with mortality.\n\nThe mean platelet volume was also higher in children with malaria compared with other medical conditions.\n\nThis may reflect early release from the bone marrow in response to peripheral platelet destruction.\n\nMicrocytosis, iron deficiency and thalassaemia in a multi-ethnic community: a pilot study.\n\nEthnicity was established by questionnaire.\n\nParasite multiplication potential and the severity of Falciparum malaria.\n\nThe rest 15 patients diagnosed with no definite etiology.\n\nConclusion: The \u03b1 -gene and s-gene mutation is quite common in the Southwest part of Iran.\n\nThalassemia and malaria: new insights into an old problem.",
